WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.710
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.630
about BigQuery Flex
Slots, Kubeflow 1.0,

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.820
and taking Next 2020 online.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.690
I'm Stephanie Wong.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.160
And welcome to
This Week in Cloud

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.650
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.120
BigQuery Reservations
can help you

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.160
handle explosive
demand for analytics

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.850
without breaking your budget.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.720
Now, BigQuery Flex Slots
take that goal even further,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.370
with a set monthly
cost that is only

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.220
billed to you for the seconds
of Flex Slots are deployed.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.530
Use Flex Slots to experiment
with your environment,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.660
plan for big events, or rapidly
respond to unexpected demand.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.790
Kubeflow provides a Kubernetes
native platform for scalable

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.710
and portable ML workloads.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.130
And thanks to the support of
its contributor community,

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.810
Kubeflow just had its
first major release.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.810
This open source project will
help you develop, build, train,

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.190
and deploy your models.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.200
And for enterprise
solutions, consider

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.870
using Kubeflow on Google
Cloud's Anthos platform

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.640
to run these machine
learning workflows

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.770
in hybrid and
multi-cloud environments.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.160
We recently introduced the
Network Intelligence Center,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.560
which offers modules
that can predict and heal

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.980
network failures.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.100
One of those modules
is connectivity test,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.560
which helps you diagnose
connectivity issues

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.380
and predict the impact
of config changes.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.510
Now, the eng leads for
this product have written

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.690
a deep dive on how the
connectivity test module works

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.030
and how you can use it
to proactively monitor

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.650
your network.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.870
In keeping with
advice from the CDC,

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.800
we are reworking Google Cloud
Next into an online experience.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.590
The dates have not changed,
April 6 through the 8,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.120
and any existing
reservations are

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.180
being converted to the
new digital connect event.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.220
We're focusing on
innovating how we interact

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.930
online with our community.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.970
So stay tuned for
more information

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.997
and be sure to
register to join us.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.080
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.540
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.370
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.870
We'll see you in the cloud.

